  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nTemperatures will remain warm through Friday with the continued\nsouthwest flow into Montana and ridge over the northern plains.\nHighs may reach the upper 90s in the southeast on Friday which\nlend to elevated Fire Weather concerns if wind gust can ramp up\nand then overlap with low RH zones. Currently, there seems to be a\nmis-match between areas of low RH in the SW and areas of strong\nwind gusts in the far northeast which are precluding Red Flag\nconditions. \n\nEarly next week as the upper ridge tilts westward and the west\ncoast trough closes off, another round of showers and\nthunderstorms is expected across the region. This is the third day\nfor a strong precipitation signal  from Sunday night into \nTuesday. While these totals could still reduce in further \nforecasts, currently a half to 1 inch is being teased at most \nlocations. The timing of this event has also backed up about 12 \nhours from previous forecasts pressing from Sunday into Monday to\nnow Sunday night into Tuesday and a drying trend is beginning to \nform in the far southeast over the Yellowstone valley.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo significant deviations from NBM were made.\n\nConfidence is HIGH through Saturday.\n\nConfidence drops to MODERATE Sunday through Tuesday.",
